. . .Second Class. . .

734
01:16:56,865 --> 01:16:59,023
. . .Carl Brashear.

735
01:17:01,370 --> 01:17:03,493
i am a Navy diver.

736
01:17:29,858 --> 01:17:31,020
Bring him up.

737
01:17:32,235 --> 01:17:33,515
-Bring him up!
-l got him.

738
01:17:34,363 --> 01:17:36,236
-We'll bring him home.
-Sailor!

739
01:17:36,490 --> 01:17:38,529
Disregard that order!

740
01:17:40,244 --> 01:17:42,035
Sailor! Sailor!

741
01:17:43,038 --> 01:17:47,747
Chief Sunday, effective immediately. . .

742
01:17:48,044 --> 01:17:51,377
. . .l am relieving you of your duties!

743
01:17:51,839 --> 01:17:53,831
Do you hear me, chief?!

744
01:17:56,845 --> 01:17:58,090
Haul in that line.

745
01:18:22,496 --> 01:18:25,497
Come on, Brashear.
You're almost there.

746
01:18:26,125 --> 01:18:27,120
A few more steps.

747
01:18:28,252 --> 01:18:29,662
Come on. We'll help you.

748
01:18:45,604 --> 01:18:46,884
Open up.

749
01:19:06,209 --> 01:19:08,415
Boatswain's Mate Carl Brashear. . .

750
01:19:09,462 --> 01:19:10,920
. . .nine hours, 31 minutes.

751
01:19:11,631 --> 01:19:13,255
Perfect assembly.

752
01:19:21,100 --> 01:19:22,345
Get him inside.

753
01:19:40,537 --> 01:19:43,740
-Carl, did, did--
-Slow down, Snowhill.

754
01:19:43,957 --> 01:19:47,242
They put me back in the program.
l start training next week.

755
01:19:47,460 --> 01:19:48,622
Congratulations.

756
01:19:49,796 --> 01:19:51,124
Thanks, Carl.

757
01:19:52,341 --> 01:19:53,336
l almost forgot.

758
01:19:53,550 --> 01:19:56,041
-You hear about Sunday?
-No.

759
01:19:56,303 --> 01:19:59,719
Mr. Pappy blew a gasket
when the son of a bitch passed you.

760
01:19:59,932 --> 01:20:02,886
He busted him down a stripe
and shipped him out.

761
01:20:03,227 --> 01:20:05,552
l guess that fucker got his
in the end.

762
01:20:07,148 --> 01:20:08,856
l guess he did.

763
01:20:15,114 --> 01:20:16,524
l guess he did.

764
01:21:22,560 --> 01:21:23,935
From the gentleman.

765
01:21:39,244 --> 01:21:40,489
You hate champagne.

766
01:21:41,914 --> 01:21:46,374
-You got a diving assignment.
-Brooklyn Navy Yard, standby diver.

767
01:21:46,585 --> 01:21:49,254
Brooklyn? Brooklyn.

768
01:21:49,630 --> 01:21:52,963
Baby, we can have dinner
like an old married couple.

769
01:21:53,176 --> 01:21:56,093
Oh, well, baby, l didn't take the job.

770
01:21:56,304 --> 01:21:58,629
We waited three years
for that slot to open up.

771
01:21:58,848 --> 01:22:01,173
l don't move up in rank unless l dive.

772
01:22:01,434 --> 01:22:03,391
l won't make master as a standby.

773
01:22:04,312 --> 01:22:06,103
l'll find something else.

774
01:22:12,112 --> 01:22:13,820
l'm three months late.

775
01:22:14,156 --> 01:22:15,354
Late for what?

776
01:22:21,455 --> 01:22:24,206
You're going to have a. . .?
A real baby?

777
01:22:25,710 --> 01:22:26,990
We're gonna have a baby!

778
01:22:27,211 --> 01:22:28,954
We're gonna have a real baby!

779
01:22:29,172 --> 01:22:30,370
We're gonna have a baby!

780
01:22:30,590 --> 01:22:34,124
Ladies, gentlemen,
and the rest of you lowdown cats. . .

781
01:22:34,427 --> 01:22:36,004
. . .it's time to ring in the New Year.

782
01:22:36,221 --> 01:22:37,929
Happy New Year.

783
01:22:41,017 --> 01:22:42,559
Happy New Year.

784
01:22:58,494 --> 01:23:00,570
You have to let them know who's boss.

785
01:23:00,830 --> 01:23:03,368
Or they'll never salute you
the rest of your life.

786
01:23:05,668 --> 01:23:06,663
Excuse me.

787
01:23:08,671 --> 01:23:11,209
What'd l tell you, hon?
He don't remember me.

788
01:23:14,761 --> 01:23:18,094
Senior Chief Sunday, U. S. S. Hoist.

789
01:23:20,851 --> 01:23:22,843
You ended my diving career,
lieutenant.

790
01:23:23,228 --> 01:23:24,259
Lieutenant Commander. . .

791
01:23:25,063 --> 01:23:27,020
. . .Hanks. Pleased to meet you.

792
01:23:27,232 --> 01:23:28,975
That was a long time ago, chief.

793
01:23:29,193 --> 01:23:30,770
Ancient history.

794
01:23:32,655 --> 01:23:36,403
Well, we just came by to say hey.

795
01:23:38,369 --> 01:23:41,156
-Auld lang syne and all.
-Auld lang syne.

796
01:23:42,290 --> 01:23:44,116
l didn't know you had a daughter.

797
01:23:44,626 --> 01:23:45,906
Right.

798
01:23:46,836 --> 01:23:48,211
She's quite lovely.

799
01:23:50,173 --> 01:23:53,506
We gotta go now,
because Billy's gonna dance with me.

800
01:23:53,719 --> 01:23:55,510
Happy New Year.

801
01:23:55,721 --> 01:23:57,263
-Have fun.
-Come on, Billy.

802
01:23:57,681 --> 01:24:00,884
You're gonna dance
with your lovely wife, right?

803
01:24:09,193 --> 01:24:11,980
See? Now wasn't that easy?

804
01:24:12,780 --> 01:24:14,856
-Has-been.
-Yes.

805
01:24:15,950 --> 01:24:18,820
No. Billy.

806
01:24:19,078 --> 01:24:21,569
He's the biggest drunk
in the Navy is all.

807
01:24:38,140 --> 01:24:39,598
Senior Chief Sunday...

808
01:24:40,434 --> 01:24:44,930
. . .you violated Article 90 of
the Uniform Code of Military Justice:

809
01:24:45,147 --> 01:24:47,388
Assaulting a superior
commission officer.

810
01:24:47,984 --> 01:24:50,985
Your conduct
is completely unacceptable.

811
01:24:51,237 --> 01:24:53,858
You're fined one half
month's pay for six months. . .

812
01:24:54,073 --> 01:24:56,943
. . .restricted to the base
for two months. . .

813
01:24:57,160 --> 01:25:00,825
. . .and are hereby reduced
in rank to chief petty officer.

814
01:25:01,498 --> 01:25:04,499
For those justjoining us,
our top story continues...

815
01:25:04,710 --> 01:25:07,711
... thousands of miles away
in the Mediterranean Sea.

816
01:25:07,963 --> 01:25:11,379
Hours ago, an American B-52 bomber
flying a routine mission...

817
01:25:11,592 --> 01:25:15,672
...over the coast of Spain
slammed into the Spanish countryside.

818
01:25:15,888 --> 01:25:20,300
Moments before, the bomber's crew
jettisoned their nuclear payload.

819
01:25:20,518 --> 01:25:23,435
Three 50-megaton
warheads parachuted to Earth.

820
01:25:23,688 --> 01:25:28,480
Two were recovered. However, a third
hydrogen bomb remains lost at sea.

821
01:25:28,693 --> 01:25:30,068
You made it.

822
01:25:30,487 --> 01:25:33,571
Becky, get your toys.
Your daddy will be home soon.

823
01:25:36,827 --> 01:25:39,662
investigating in deep water
will be the work ofAL ViN...

824
01:25:39,871 --> 01:25:43,868
...a two-man submersible on loan from
Woods Hole Oceanographic institute.

825
01:25:44,084 --> 01:25:48,128
As Navy ships comb the Mediterranean
in search of the warhead...

826
01:25:48,339 --> 01:25:50,130
...so do Russian submarines.

827
01:25:50,341 --> 01:25:54,125
Since the bomb disappeared
in international waters...

828
01:25:54,345 --> 01:25:56,254
...it belongs to whoever finds it.

829
01:25:56,764 --> 01:25:59,385
Charged with locating it
before the Soviets...

830
01:25:59,600 --> 01:26:02,684
...are the elite Navy deep-sea divers
pictured here.

831
01:26:02,896 --> 01:26:07,356
Stationed in Norfolk, Virginia, the
divers were flown here hours ago...

832
01:26:07,567 --> 01:26:11,185
...many still dressed in the uniforms
they had on this morning.

833
01:26:22,249 --> 01:26:23,909
Blue diver, this is captain.

834
01:26:28,381 --> 01:26:29,626
Blue diver, come in.

835
01:26:30,967 --> 01:26:32,876
l'm here, Hart. What do you need?

836
01:26:34,053 --> 01:26:37,671
Carl, i'd appreciate it if you could
find my lost nuke for me.

837
01:26:37,891 --> 01:26:40,216
i'd like to make admiral before i die.

838
01:26:40,435 --> 01:26:42,427
l'm doing my best, Hart.

839
01:27:10,800 --> 01:27:14,251
l have an unidentified metal object
protruding from the bottom.

840
01:27:14,471 --> 01:27:16,712
He has something.
Proceed with caution.

841
01:27:16,931 --> 01:27:18,389
Roger that.

842
01:27:27,818 --> 01:27:30,106
Topside, we have a Coke can.

843
01:27:30,779 --> 01:27:32,487
Goddamn Coke can.

844
01:27:32,990 --> 01:27:36,406
Bring it up anyway, chief.
i like my ocean clean.

845
01:27:41,457 --> 01:27:43,330
Turn sonar off. A diver's down--

846
01:27:43,543 --> 01:27:45,950
-That's not our sonar.
-What?

847
01:27:47,797 --> 01:27:48,911
Shit.

848
01:27:50,467 --> 01:27:52,673
Alpha Whiskey, this is Charlie Victor.

849
01:27:52,886 --> 01:27:55,721
l've got an unknown object.
Probable submarine.

850
01:27:57,474 --> 01:27:59,597
Blue diver,
we have an unknown contact.

851
01:27:59,810 --> 01:28:02,135
Probable Russian sub.
Bearing at 209...

852
01:28:02,354 --> 01:28:05,308
...at 16 knots
and headed directly for you.

853
01:28:05,524 --> 01:28:08,774
Take immediate evasive action.
immediate evasive action.

854
01:28:08,986 --> 01:28:12,900
Prepare for emergency surface.
Blue diver, do you hear me?

855
01:28:13,115 --> 01:28:14,194
Do you hear me?

856
01:28:14,408 --> 01:28:15,439
Blue diver?

857
01:28:19,038 --> 01:28:20,318
Talk to me, Carl.

858
01:28:50,530 --> 01:28:51,810
Talk to me, Carl.

859
01:29:05,045 --> 01:29:06,076
Come in, blue diver.

860
01:29:16,390 --> 01:29:18,466
Tell the dive station
to supply a standby.

861
01:29:20,561 --> 01:29:21,971
Come in, Carl.

862
01:29:32,574 --> 01:29:34,198
Come on, Carl.

863
01:29:53,095 --> 01:29:54,803
Carl, do you read me?

864
01:29:55,723 --> 01:29:56,837
l'm here, captain.

865
01:29:57,808 --> 01:29:58,839
He's there.

866
01:29:59,518 --> 01:30:02,435
Prepare to surface, Carl.
We're bringing you home.

867
01:30:11,823 --> 01:30:16,485
Next time you scare the shit out of me
give me a courtesy warning first.

868
01:30:27,923 --> 01:30:30,877
Captain, the sub kicked up
half the ocean bottom.

869
01:30:31,093 --> 01:30:32,468
lt found it for us!

870
01:30:33,095 --> 01:30:34,174
You're kidding.

871
01:30:35,348 --> 01:30:36,676
Oh, yeah!

872
01:30:36,974 --> 01:30:38,219
He thinks he found it.

873
01:30:38,851 --> 01:30:40,760
Yeah, you got it. That's it.

874
01:30:43,982 --> 01:30:45,144
Steady!

875
01:30:45,817 --> 01:30:49,316
Steady. Let's take it in.
Bring it up.

876
01:30:58,831 --> 01:31:00,159
Let's go now.

877
01:31:16,975 --> 01:31:18,006
Move!

878
01:32:21,375 --> 01:32:22,406
Jo.

879
01:32:32,637 --> 01:32:34,546
l was so scared.

880
01:32:34,764 --> 01:32:36,306
l'm sorry.

881
01:32:43,607 --> 01:32:45,350
Oh, shit.

882
01:32:49,780 --> 01:32:51,274
Your leg. . .

883
01:32:51,782 --> 01:32:53,608
. . .was nearly severed.

884
01:32:56,454 --> 01:32:58,493
lt's gonna take time to heal.

885
01:33:00,792 --> 01:33:04,955
Eventually, you're gonna be able
to walk again, with a cane.

886
01:33:08,008 --> 01:33:09,751
Can l still dive?

887
01:33:12,804 --> 01:33:14,464
l'm so sorry.

888
01:33:50,677 --> 01:33:52,468
Come home, Carl.

889
01:34:00,688 --> 01:34:04,388
Your husband was found drunk
on a public beach this morning.

890
01:34:04,609 --> 01:34:09,187
He's an alcoholic and must remain here
in detox for 30 days.

891
01:34:09,405 --> 01:34:12,359
lf he should stagger,
he will not fall!

892
01:34:12,575 --> 01:34:15,825
lf he should fall,
he will fall in such a manner. . .

893
01:34:16,037 --> 01:34:17,317
. . .as to cover up his rate. . .

894
01:34:17,581 --> 01:34:21,032
. . .so that passersby will think
he is an officer!

895
01:34:23,754 --> 01:34:26,161
A chief petty officer shall not drink.

896
01:34:26,381 --> 01:34:29,832
However, if he should drink,
he shall not get drunk.

897
01:34:30,052 --> 01:34:33,836
lf he should get drunk,
he shall not stagger!

898
01:34:34,056 --> 01:34:37,140
lf he should stagger,
he shall not fall!

899
01:34:37,351 --> 01:34:40,885
And if he should fall,
he will fall in such a manner. . .

900
01:34:41,105 --> 01:34:44,770
. . .as to cover up his rate, so
passersby will think he's an officer!

901
01:34:46,528 --> 01:34:49,482
We're all extremely proud of you,
Chief Brashear.

902
01:34:49,698 --> 01:34:54,360
Now get better so you can go home
and enjoy your retirement.

903
01:34:54,578 --> 01:34:55,740
Give us a smile, chief.

904
01:34:55,954 --> 01:34:59,488
-How will you spend retirement?
-How's it feel to be a hero?

905
01:35:20,521 --> 01:35:21,766
Hey, you.

906
01:36:02,482 --> 01:36:03,680
Sweetheart. . .

907
01:36:09,114 --> 01:36:10,822
. . .you'll never dive again.

908
01:36:15,663 --> 01:36:17,536
And what you gotta do now. . .

909
01:36:18,499 --> 01:36:20,372
. . .l can't help you with.

910
01:36:26,007 --> 01:36:27,964
But when you're ready to leave. . .

911
01:36:28,384 --> 01:36:33,211
. . .and if you can promise me you'll
never take another drink again. . .

912
01:36:33,681 --> 01:36:36,847
. . .l'll be waiting for you
in that car over there.

913
01:36:41,064 --> 01:36:42,641
But if you can't. . .

914
01:36:49,073 --> 01:36:50,946
. . .then you just walk on by.

915
01:37:35,997 --> 01:37:37,372
Package for you, sir.

916
01:38:00,648 --> 01:38:02,391
i want to come back.

917
01:38:03,067 --> 01:38:05,818
-To where, chief?
-Full diving duty.

918
01:38:06,612 --> 01:38:08,272
l want to dive again.

919
01:38:08,531 --> 01:38:10,108
Carl. . .

920
01:38:10,450 --> 01:38:12,775
-. . .l understand but. . . .
-But. . .

921
01:38:13,536 --> 01:38:15,327
. . .it's just not possible.

922
01:38:16,664 --> 01:38:18,455
Good afternoon, admiral.

923
01:38:18,875 --> 01:38:21,116
-Carl, this is--
-Captain Hanks.

924
01:38:21,461 --> 01:38:22,409
Chief Brashear.

925
01:38:22,712 --> 01:38:25,285
Captain Hanks is the senior officer. . .

926
01:38:25,507 --> 01:38:29,339
. . .of the Personnel Policy
Control Board at the Pentagon.

927
01:38:29,553 --> 01:38:31,095
He'll be with us a few weeks. . .

928
01:38:31,305 --> 01:38:34,804
. . .meeting some of the men from the
front lines, hearing their concerns.

929
01:38:35,059 --> 01:38:37,597
To return to the chief's
primary concern.

930
01:38:37,812 --> 01:38:41,940
Working as a Navy diver
with one good leg and the other. . . .

931
01:38:42,608 --> 01:38:44,980
l'm sorry, it's just not possible.

932
01:38:45,194 --> 01:38:46,225
Cut it off.

933
01:38:50,033 --> 01:38:53,817
''lnjured pilots have requested
amputation of injured limbs.

934
01:38:54,037 --> 01:38:57,156
With a prosthesis,
several have returned to duty. ''

935
01:38:58,500 --> 01:38:59,614
l'm asking this:

936
01:38:59,835 --> 01:39:04,793
Cut off my leg and assemble a medical
review board 1 2 weeks from today.

937
01:39:05,007 --> 01:39:09,087
Then l will demonstrate that l am fit
to return to full diving duty.

938
01:39:09,762 --> 01:39:11,671
l want to make master chief.

939
01:39:14,517 --> 01:39:18,466
We admire your courage, chief,
however misplaced it may be.

940
01:39:18,688 --> 01:39:20,230
Please excuse us.

941
01:39:31,451 --> 01:39:33,194
l am a doctor, Carl.

942
01:39:33,578 --> 01:39:36,033
My opinion might mean something here.

943
01:39:39,877 --> 01:39:41,335
l guess not.

944
01:39:43,547 --> 01:39:45,705
How will you come back with one leg?

945
01:39:46,258 --> 01:39:48,250
l could barely read once.
l found a way.

946
01:39:51,722 --> 01:39:54,509
l could put up with the months
at sea. . .

947
01:39:55,518 --> 01:39:57,890
. . .the dangerous assignments
you never refused.

948
01:39:58,104 --> 01:40:00,061
-But this?
-What do you want from me?

949
01:40:01,483 --> 01:40:05,646
That l come home, mow the lawn,
put a wheelchair ramp in?

950
01:40:06,321 --> 01:40:09,690
-How am l gonna look at my son?
-Leave him out of this.

951
01:40:10,701 --> 01:40:14,829
You're not doing this for him or me.
This is about you.

952
01:40:15,289 --> 01:40:17,447
lt's always been about you.

953
01:40:18,792 --> 01:40:20,369
Admit it, Carl.

954
01:40:21,462 --> 01:40:24,035
At least give me that much.

955
01:40:34,058 --> 01:40:36,430
Why are you doing this to me?

956
01:40:41,483 --> 01:40:43,025
Answer me, goddamn it!

957
01:40:43,485 --> 01:40:47,317
Or l'm walking out of here
and l am not coming back.

958
01:41:21,733 --> 01:41:23,227
l love you, Jo.

959
01:43:45,843 --> 01:43:47,919
Get away! Get away from me!

960
01:43:48,137 --> 01:43:49,465
Piece of shit!

961
01:43:51,557 --> 01:43:52,636
Cookie.

962
01:43:54,560 --> 01:43:58,011
Goddamn. Looks like l missed
one hell of a party.

963
01:44:04,737 --> 01:44:06,445
l've been all over.

964
01:44:07,031 --> 01:44:08,573
Trouble, mostly.

965
01:44:08,825 --> 01:44:12,407
Navy gave me a second-class diving
school in Little Creek.

966
01:44:12,621 --> 01:44:14,329
Don't amount to shit.

967
01:44:18,544 --> 01:44:20,370
l made some calls.

968
01:44:22,381 --> 01:44:23,958
On Friday, that Captain Hanks. . .

969
01:44:24,174 --> 01:44:27,792
. . .is convening a medical review board
and he's gonna retire you.

970
01:44:30,306 --> 01:44:33,057
-He said l had 4 weeks.
-He lied, Cookie.

971
01:44:33,351 --> 01:44:36,601
He don't care how many one-legged
pushups you can do.

972
01:44:36,854 --> 01:44:39,890
He'd trade you and me
and every other sea dog. . .

973
01:44:40,150 --> 01:44:42,557
. . .for one glass-eyed
electronics technician.

974
01:44:42,777 --> 01:44:44,686
The man's gonna retire your ass.

975
01:44:44,905 --> 01:44:46,696
My leg's back. l ain't done yet.

976
01:44:46,907 --> 01:44:50,406
You got a stump on a stick
and no chance of beating Hanks, son.

977
01:44:56,250 --> 01:45:00,330
-All l wanted was to be master diver.
-All l wanted was to stay one.

978
01:45:02,631 --> 01:45:05,300
You want to beat Hanks,
you got to go around him. . .

979
01:45:05,509 --> 01:45:07,133
. . .right to the top.

980
01:45:08,095 --> 01:45:09,090
Washington.

981
01:45:10,765 --> 01:45:13,884
-Chief of naval personnel.
-That's right.

982
01:45:14,644 --> 01:45:17,977
They don't like cocky pencil pushers
like Hanks any more than we do.

983
01:45:21,401 --> 01:45:23,440
l might be able to pull a few strings.

984
01:45:30,160 --> 01:45:32,152
Why are you doing this, Sunday?

985
01:45:35,708 --> 01:45:37,368
Piss people off.

986
01:45:37,960 --> 01:45:40,914
Chief Decker, you are
the chief master at arms. . .

987
01:45:41,130 --> 01:45:42,458
. . .of this hospital?

988
01:45:42,715 --> 01:45:43,663
Yes, sir.

989
01:45:45,968 --> 01:45:49,800
Then why is it you don't know
where Chief Brashear is?

990
01:45:50,515 --> 01:45:52,472
He shouldn't be too hard to spot.

991
01:45:52,684 --> 01:45:56,218
He's the only negro diver
in the Navy. . .

992
01:45:56,438 --> 01:45:58,062
. . .and he's got one leg.

993
01:45:58,648 --> 01:46:02,515
lt seems that the chief
has transferred, sir.

994
01:46:04,196 --> 01:46:06,734
-On whose orders?
-He signed his own, sir.

995
01:46:08,701 --> 01:46:09,899
Call the shore patrol.

996
01:46:10,119 --> 01:46:12,158
Relax, cap. We just want to talk.

997
01:46:13,789 --> 01:46:14,903
Wait, wait, wait.

998
01:46:15,499 --> 01:46:17,824
You know where Chief Brashear is.
Where?

999
01:46:20,546 --> 01:46:22,585
l see. Fine.

1000
01:46:22,799 --> 01:46:26,168
Chief Brashear is AWOL.
l want him found and arrested now.

1001
01:46:26,428 --> 01:46:27,838
You ain't gonna find him.

1002
01:46:29,180 --> 01:46:30,342
What do you want?

1003
01:46:30,557 --> 01:46:34,257
Four weeks to train him,
then a reinstatement hearing. . .

1004
01:46:34,478 --> 01:46:36,102
. . .with the chief of naval personnel.

1005
01:46:37,022 --> 01:46:39,014
-The chief of. . .?
-Yes, sir.

1006
01:46:39,233 --> 01:46:40,857
-ln Washington?
-That's right.

1007
01:46:41,443 --> 01:46:42,818
Forget it.

1008
01:46:49,410 --> 01:46:52,280
-Will the diver be reinstated?
-Will he get a hearing?

1009
01:46:52,538 --> 01:46:56,785
Seems Chief Brashear losing his leg
for his country makes him a hero, sir.

1010
01:46:57,502 --> 01:46:58,581
Fine.

1011
01:47:03,508 --> 01:47:05,631
l will grant you your hearing. . .

1012
01:47:06,094 --> 01:47:07,469
. . .on one condition.

1013
01:47:08,513 --> 01:47:11,430
When he fails, you retire.

1014
01:47:11,975 --> 01:47:13,635
He ain't gonna fail.

1015
01:47:59,442 --> 01:48:01,351
Minute five faster.

1016
01:48:04,947 --> 01:48:06,357
See you in court.

1017
01:49:43,884 --> 01:49:46,209
Captain Hanks ordered you
to remain here, chief.

1018
01:50:12,539 --> 01:50:15,030
Please be seated,
Senior Chief Brashear.

1019
01:50:21,048 --> 01:50:23,621
Only the Army salutes indoors,
senior chief.

1020
01:50:23,843 --> 01:50:26,381
The Navy l grew up in
warrants a salute. . .

1021
01:50:26,596 --> 01:50:28,422
. . .given the gravity
of this occasion.

1022
01:50:28,640 --> 01:50:29,838
Well. . .

1023
01:50:31,101 --> 01:50:32,892
. . .we're in a new Navy now.

1024
01:50:39,026 --> 01:50:40,271
Shall we begin?

1025
01:50:46,951 --> 01:50:49,524
Do you honestly feel that,
as a man. . . .

1026
01:50:52,581 --> 01:50:54,075
You're almost 40.

1027
01:50:54,375 --> 01:50:56,201
You have one leg.

1028
01:50:56,502 --> 01:51:00,120
Can you really keep up
with healthy divers half your age?

1029
01:51:00,965 --> 01:51:02,791
The question is, sir:

1030
01:51:03,134 --> 01:51:04,711
Can they keep up with me?

1031
01:51:11,309 --> 01:51:12,637
No smoking, chief.

1032
01:51:29,036 --> 01:51:33,496
Navy diving studies indicate that
if a subject were to become. . .

1033
01:51:33,708 --> 01:51:36,329
. . .unconscious or deceased. . .

1034
01:51:36,544 --> 01:51:40,624
. . .the disparity between the buoyancy
of a prosthetic. . .

1035
01:51:40,840 --> 01:51:43,959
. . .and a limb would hinder him
in a free dive mode.

1036
01:51:44,177 --> 01:51:47,759
You mean if he drowned,
he wouldn't float right, yes?

1037
01:51:49,016 --> 01:51:52,515
Sirs, l promise
if l am killed at sea. . .

1038
01:51:52,770 --> 01:51:55,343
. . .l will make every effort
to die like a Navy man.

1039
01:52:21,550 --> 01:52:24,551
You should see the future
of Navy deep-sea diving.

1040
01:52:24,761 --> 01:52:27,252
This is the latest He/O2,
mixed gas rig.

1041
01:52:27,473 --> 01:52:29,050
lt weighs 290 pounds.

1042
01:52:29,266 --> 01:52:34,177
Men who want to use it, before
starting diving training, must walk. . .

1043
01:52:34,396 --> 01:52:37,147
. . .twelve steps unassisted.

1044
01:52:39,151 --> 01:52:41,558
Could you do that,
Senior Chief Brashear?

1045
01:52:48,787 --> 01:52:49,949
Yes, sir, l could.

1046
01:52:51,373 --> 01:52:52,404
Well. . .

1047
01:52:52,707 --> 01:52:53,905
. . .l see.

1048
01:52:54,751 --> 01:52:56,245
Much as l hate to prolong this. . .

1049
01:52:56,503 --> 01:52:59,587
. . .in the interest of thoroughness,
l'll make arrangements. . .

1050
01:52:59,798 --> 01:53:01,292
. . .for you to demonstrate.

1051
01:53:01,508 --> 01:53:02,670
Here, sir.

1052
01:53:03,260 --> 01:53:04,374
Now.

1053
01:53:05,429 --> 01:53:08,264
Son, step aside,
or l'll crack you in the jaw.

1054
01:53:11,811 --> 01:53:16,354
-This is hardly the appropriate venue.
-l want them all to see, sir.

1055
01:53:17,233 --> 01:53:19,854
Captain, l concur
with your assessment.

1056
01:53:24,282 --> 01:53:26,820
These slippery floors prohibit
a demonstration.

1057
01:53:27,035 --> 01:53:29,360
Haven't you had enough career trouble?

1058
01:53:29,955 --> 01:53:32,113
Your advice and presence
are unwelcome.

1059
01:53:32,499 --> 01:53:35,453
-Who is this man?
-Chief Leslie W. Sunday, sir.

1060
01:53:36,503 --> 01:53:40,002
You swam out of the Saint Lo
at Leyte Gulf.

1061
01:53:41,759 --> 01:53:43,134
Held your breath for. . .

1062
01:53:44,470 --> 01:53:46,296
-. . .four minutes.
-Five, sir.

1063
01:53:49,934 --> 01:53:51,048
He can stay.

1064
01:53:53,646 --> 01:53:56,219
Fine. lrrelevant.

1065
01:53:57,108 --> 01:54:00,358
Gentlemen, sirs, returning
to the issue at hand. . .

1066
01:54:00,695 --> 01:54:04,692
. . .this is not the time or place
for Senior Chief Bra--

1067
01:54:06,660 --> 01:54:09,364
Excuse me, senior chief.
ls there a problem?

1068
01:54:13,375 --> 01:54:14,370
Captain Hanks. . .

1069
01:54:15,544 --> 01:54:18,877
. . .l've spent my life in the Navy
trying only to succeed.

1070
01:54:19,340 --> 01:54:22,839
But my quest has caused great
personal loss to those who love me.

1071
01:54:23,511 --> 01:54:25,468
They too have made sacrifices.

1072
01:54:25,680 --> 01:54:28,681
They too have endured
great pains to support me.

1073
01:54:28,933 --> 01:54:31,424
lf l walk these 1 2 steps today. . .

1074
01:54:31,811 --> 01:54:34,052
. . .reinstate me to active duty.

1075
01:54:34,606 --> 01:54:36,183
Give me my career back.

1076
01:54:36,650 --> 01:54:39,935
Let me finish it,
and go home in peace.

1077
01:54:43,073 --> 01:54:46,323
Senior Chief Brashear,
the business of the modern Navy--

1078
01:54:46,535 --> 01:54:50,484
Forgive me, sir, but to me
the Navy is not a business.

1079
01:54:50,748 --> 01:54:54,448
We have many traditions. ln my
career, l've experienced most of them.

1080
01:54:54,668 --> 01:54:57,123
Some good, some bad.

1081
01:54:57,421 --> 01:55:01,205
However, l wouldn't be here today
if not for our greatest tradition.

1082
01:55:02,427 --> 01:55:03,969
And which one is that?

1083
01:55:05,555 --> 01:55:06,800
Honor, sir.

1084
01:55:15,732 --> 01:55:18,187
Get on with it, senior chief.

1085
01:55:21,738 --> 01:55:23,066
Leslie?

1086
01:55:24,908 --> 01:55:26,450
What leg you got on?

1087
01:55:26,994 --> 01:55:28,571
My walking leg. . .

1088
01:55:28,788 --> 01:55:30,033
. . .Leslie.

1089
01:55:30,247 --> 01:55:31,871
lt was my dad's name.
Got a problem?

1090
01:55:32,083 --> 01:55:34,574
Oh, no, no problem at all.

1091
01:55:41,259 --> 01:55:44,343
That thing's light duty.
lt'll snap like a matchstick.

1092
01:55:44,554 --> 01:55:47,757
-l'll put my weight on my good leg.
-290 pounds on one leg?

1093
01:55:47,974 --> 01:55:50,928
You'll be passed out by the sixth step.

1094
01:55:53,105 --> 01:55:55,311
Tenders, hat the diver.

1095
01:56:44,951 --> 01:56:46,943
Navy diver, stand up.

1096
01:56:48,955 --> 01:56:50,069
Leave him.

1097
01:56:51,624 --> 01:56:56,202
Captain, if l recall Navy regulations,
the diver may be helped to his feet.

1098
01:56:57,297 --> 01:57:00,001
lt's a lot of brass to sling up
from a seated position.

1099
01:57:00,717 --> 01:57:04,133
lt's spun copper, chief.
We haven't used brass in a decade.

1100
01:57:04,346 --> 01:57:07,845
The new manual states the diver
must rise unassisted.

1101
01:57:08,058 --> 01:57:10,050
That's what it says in the new book?

1102
01:57:11,562 --> 01:57:14,765
lf l may ask, captain,
how would you know?

1103
01:57:15,441 --> 01:57:16,603
l wrote it.

1104
01:57:20,780 --> 01:57:22,155
Yes, sir.

1105
01:57:27,620 --> 01:57:28,568
Navy diver. . .

1106
01:57:28,788 --> 01:57:30,198
. . .stand up.

1107
01:57:39,883 --> 01:57:42,552
Square that rig and approach the rail.

1108
01:58:03,450 --> 01:58:04,445
One.

1109
01:58:07,287 --> 01:58:08,318
Two.

1110
01:58:11,500 --> 01:58:12,531
Three.

1111
01:58:16,171 --> 01:58:17,166
Four.

1112
01:58:20,467 --> 01:58:21,498
Five.

1113
01:58:24,764 --> 01:58:25,759
Six.

1114
01:58:27,767 --> 01:58:28,762
Seven.

1115
01:58:31,938 --> 01:58:32,851
Eight.

1116
01:58:38,820 --> 01:58:39,934
Gentlemen, his leg.

1117
01:58:41,281 --> 01:58:42,360
Please.

1118
01:58:43,492 --> 01:58:44,487
Gentlemen.

1119
01:58:46,662 --> 01:58:49,616
-Navy diver, stand down.
-Diver, you will disregard.

1120
01:58:49,998 --> 01:58:51,789
-This is my detail.
-Admiral?

1121
01:58:54,295 --> 01:58:57,628
Goddamn it, Cookie, move your ass!
l want my 1 2.

1122
01:59:09,686 --> 01:59:12,058
Nine. The Navy diver
is not a fighting man.

1123
01:59:12,272 --> 01:59:14,311
He is a salvage expert.

1124
01:59:15,150 --> 01:59:17,723
Ten. lf it's lost underwater,
he finds it.

1125
01:59:17,944 --> 01:59:19,521
lf it's sunk, he brings it up.

1126
01:59:19,738 --> 01:59:22,229
lf it's in the way, he moves it.

1127
01:59:22,658 --> 01:59:27,450
Eleven. lf he's lucky, he'll die
young, 200 feet beneath the waves.

1128
01:59:27,663 --> 01:59:30,617
For that is the closest
he will ever get to being a hero.

1129
01:59:30,833 --> 01:59:34,036
Hell, l don't know why anyone
would want to be a Navy diver.

1130
01:59:34,253 --> 01:59:36,922
Now you report to this line, Cookie.

1131
01:59:41,552 --> 01:59:43,295
At ease.

1132
01:59:56,401 --> 01:59:58,061
Tenders, unhat that diver.

1133
02:00:20,760 --> 02:00:23,796
The United States Navy
proudly reinstates. . .

1134
02:00:24,472 --> 02:00:26,263
. . .senior chief and diver. . .

1135
02:00:27,058 --> 02:00:30,890
. . .Carl Brashear to full active duty.

1136
02:00:51,084 --> 02:00:52,115
Thank you.

1137
02:01:07,851 --> 02:01:09,226
l can quit.

1138
02:01:09,812 --> 02:01:13,263
The man l married never quit anything
a day in his life.

1139
02:01:17,570 --> 02:01:18,815
l love you.

1140
02:01:19,030 --> 02:01:22,862
l love you too, baby.
l love you too.



